    "message": "feat(reality): implement Q23 Accept-path - reality certificate with per-handshake HMAC signature\n\ncrypto-core: LABEL_REALITY_CERT, derive_reality_auth_key (X25519 + HKDF-SHA256),\nreality_cert_signature (HMAC-SHA512) with deterministic vectors, domain separation\nfrom K_probe_fleet, and RFC 7748 clamp sensitivity tests.\n\ncover-reality: RealityCertState (per-process rcgen Ed25519 skeleton, PKCS#8 v1\nconversion for boring), build_reality_cert (signatureValue overwrite in DER),\nparse of public key_share from ClientHello (x25519 = 0x001D), AcceptServer\n(select-certificate callback with per-handshake cert substitution). Tests:\nunit roundtrip without T1 + ignored live loopback TLS 1.3 handshake with real\nboring client (x25519 keyshare + ed25519 sigalgs).\n\nDocs: T1 entry in QUESTIONS.md (client keyshare access - blocks e2e, not server),\nrcgen ledger in DEPENDENCIES.md, design 03/05 updated.\n\n🤖 Generated with Codebuff\nCo-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>",
